    "turns": [
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "If we take PaLM-E apart, which idea truly changed the direction of research?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial-hook"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "Robotic learning systems often used task-specific policies, while large language models showed broad transfer across textual tasks. PaLM-E asked whether sensor observations could enter a language model directly so that embodied tasks share the same general-purpose reasoning substrate.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-primary-record"],
            "claimIds": [
                "claim-annual-membership",
                "claim-publication-record",
                "claim-contributor-record",
                "claim-multimodal-sentence",
                "claim-positive-transfer"
            ],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.historical-background"
        },
        {
            "role": "A",
            "text": "That sounds like a promising direction. What mechanism actually makes it work?",
            "sourceIds": [],
            "claimIds": [],
            "contentOrigin": "editorial"
        },
        {
            "role": "B",
            "text": "Images and robot states are encoded as continuous embeddings and placed into a multimodal sentence alongside ordinary text tokens. The language model then predicts text that can express answers, plans or high-level decisions, while joint training mixes robotics data with vision-language and language tasks.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-primary-record"],
            "claimIds": [
                "claim-annual-membership",
                "claim-publication-record",
                "claim-contributor-record",
                "claim-multimodal-sentence",
                "claim-positive-transfer"
            ],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.core-idea"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "Experts generally treat PaLM-E as an early large-scale bridge between embodied AI and multimodal language modeling. Its formulation influenced later vision-language-action systems by showing that robot observations and general web-scale knowledge can coexist inside one sequence model.",
            "sourceIds": ["source-primary-record"],
            "claimIds": [
                "claim-annual-membership",
                "claim-publication-record",
                "claim-contributor-record",
                "claim-multimodal-sentence",
                "claim-positive-transfer"
            ],
            "contentOrigin": "commentarySections.long-term-legacy"
        },
        {
            "role": "N",
            "text": "Seen alongside LLaVA, PaLM-E reveals how the same technical question can echo across different eras.",
            "sourceIds": [
                "source-primary-record",
                "source-openalex-record",
